From a0de45b3a178e3ef681835da9a3766a1198dd728 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): sparse MLA stage-1 KV gather and staging barrier
 opt

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (Local Inference Lab integration/karmic-kraken-beta, patch 0761 head 320021e3c4db)

Rationale:
1. In Sparse MLA Stage 1 (decode_body), slot resolution ran a 4-iteration serial loop (for c in T.serial(G)) calling gather_swa(..., BI=32) or gather_idx(..., BI=32), which executed on a single warp (32 threads) while the remaining 3 or 7 warps waited at __syncthreads(), serializing 4 waves of dependent IdxIndices -> IdxPageTable loads. When swa_blocks % G == 0, each segment is purely SWA or purely indexed; gathering all G * BI = 128 slots in one parallel call across 4 warps issues all 128 page-table lookups in a single parallel wave.
2. Staging 288-byte indexed KV records (18 x 16B segments) into a [32, 528] shared buffer required non-power-of-two (/ 9) * 528 + (% 18) * 16 shared-memory offset arithmetic on every cp.async and dequant_idx load. Rounding SWA staging rows up to a multiple of 6 (swa_rows = 36, 36 * 528 = 66 * 288 = 19,008 B) and viewing the same shared buffer as [66, 288] collapses indexed cp.async destination offsets to linear 16-byte thread indices ((k * threads + tx) * 16).
3. In decode_body, reading copy_slot[k] = slots[...] after dequant_chunk + T.sync_threads() caused TileLang's ThreadSync pass to insert an extra __syncthreads() before issuing cp.async for chunk + 1. Splitting stage_chunk into load_copy_slots and issue_stage_chunk and preloading copy_slot for chunk + 1 before ptx_wait_group(0) eliminates that barrier.
4. In chunk_update, re-reading slots[base + i] >= 0 from dynamic shared memory after T.reduce_max wrote to shared workspace emitted 4 shared-memory loads and an extra __syncthreads() per chunk. Checking acc_s[h, i] != -T.infinity(accum_dtype) in registers eliminates both the shared-memory loads and the barrier (reducing decode_body barriers from 10 to 8 per chunk) while preserving NaN propagation for selected keys.
5. In extend_body, bounding the outer segment loop by active_segs = (swa_blocks // G) + min(cdiv(max(IdxLengths[row], 0), G * BI), segments - (swa_blocks // G)) skips trailing inactive indexed segments on short contexts (-52% latency at idx_len=64) with zero inner-loop branch overhead at full context.

Quality implications:
- Bit-identical (torch.equal) outputs across split, decode, and extend routes for all head counts (TP=3 24 heads, TP=4 16 heads, TP=1 64 heads), SWA-only and indexed layers, and ragged context lengths.

Tests:
- pytest -p tests.kernels.deepseek_v41_pdl_sources tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py -k 'sparse_mla or wo_input'

Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 SM121 TileLang attention kernel optimization.
